# Files Vercel must not receive.
#
# The first entry is the load-bearing one: Vercel's Python runtime treats a
# root-level app.py as the application entrypoint, and app.py here is the
# Streamlit UI, which cannot run on a serverless function at all. Keeping it
# out of the upload means Vercel resolves the file-based function in api/
# instead. app.py is the Render deployment's entrypoint and is unaffected.
app.py
.streamlit/
cli.py

# Only requirements.txt (python-docx) is needed to run the function. The
# Streamlit and spaCy extras would add ~250 MB to the bundle for no benefit.
requirements-app.txt
requirements-ner.txt
render.yaml

# Not reachable from the function.
evaluation/
tests/
data/
*.md
.gitignore

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
